WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.701 --> 00:00:02.635
Now to our breaking news.

00:00:02.635 --> 00:00:05.071
A Russian jet has forced down a U.S.

00:00:05.071 --> 00:00:08.108
drone over the Black Sea
after damaging its propeller.

00:00:08.375 --> 00:00:12.178
CNN's Oren Liebermann is at the Pentagon
gathering details on this.

00:00:12.412 --> 00:00:14.614
Oren,
tell us what we're learning about this.

00:00:15.382 --> 00:00:17.050
Brianna,
this played out early this morning

00:00:17.050 --> 00:00:18.718
over international waters
of the Black Sea.

00:00:18.718 --> 00:00:22.522
According to the U.S., Air Force
Europe, an MQ nine Reaper drone, a U.S.

00:00:22.522 --> 00:00:26.793
Air Force surveillance drone or a spy
drone was flying over the Black Sea when,

00:00:26.793 --> 00:00:29.796
according to the Air Force,
two Russian fighter jets conducted what

00:00:29.796 --> 00:00:33.066
they're calling an unsafe
and unprofessional interception.

00:00:33.299 --> 00:00:34.567
That's just the beginning of it.

00:00:34.567 --> 00:00:39.105
According to the Air Force,
the two Russian SU 27 flanker fighter jets

00:00:39.272 --> 00:00:43.376
repeatedly flew in front of the MQ nine
Reaper drone, apparently in an attempt

00:00:43.376 --> 00:00:48.481
to disrupt or disturb its flight pattern,
even dumping fuel in front of that U.S.

00:00:48.481 --> 00:00:49.382
Reaper drone.

00:00:49.382 --> 00:00:53.286
And then according to the Air Force,
one of those SU 27 fighter jets

00:00:53.620 --> 00:00:56.623
damaged the propeller of the Reaper drone
forcing it down

00:00:56.823 --> 00:00:58.491
the propeller on a reaper is behind it.

00:00:58.491 --> 00:01:02.062
So somehow that Russian fighter jet
managed to damage the propeller,

00:01:02.228 --> 00:01:03.063
forcing the U.S.

00:01:03.063 --> 00:01:05.832
to bring down the drone
in international waters.

00:01:05.865 --> 00:01:08.902
Of course,
this is a very severe incident and U.S.

00:01:08.902 --> 00:01:10.470
Air Force Europe issued a statement

00:01:10.470 --> 00:01:13.773
essentially essentially referencing
how severely they view this.

00:01:13.773 --> 00:01:15.508
Let me read you a part of this.

00:01:15.508 --> 00:01:17.710
This incident demonstrates
a lack of competence.

00:01:17.944 --> 00:01:20.313
In addition
to being unsafe and unprofessional.

00:01:20.313 --> 00:01:23.650
These aggressive actions
by Russian air crew are dangerous

00:01:23.650 --> 00:01:27.087
and could lead to miscalculation
and unintended escalation.

00:01:27.120 --> 00:01:29.022
According to the national security
Council.

00:01:29.022 --> 00:01:32.025
President Joe Biden was briefed
on the incident earlier this morning

00:01:32.292 --> 00:01:34.427
by national security
adviser Jake Sullivan.

00:01:34.427 --> 00:01:37.063
So he was given that information
about how this played out.

00:01:37.363 --> 00:01:41.434
Earlier today, according to the NSC,
there have been other interceptions

00:01:41.968 --> 00:01:43.436
between Russian and U.S.

00:01:43.436 --> 00:01:47.674
aircraft, but none as severe
or as potentially escalatory

00:01:47.674 --> 00:01:52.011
as this where we see an actual collision
in midair between a Russian fighter

00:01:52.011 --> 00:01:55.048
jet and a US drone
that forced down the US drone.

00:01:55.181 --> 00:01:57.684
Of course, the key question now, Brianna,
how does the U.S.

00:01:57.684 --> 00:02:01.888
respond How severely do they view this
and how deliberately do they view this?

00:02:02.088 --> 00:02:03.423
Certainly the statement from U.S.

00:02:03.423 --> 00:02:04.090
Air Force

00:02:04.090 --> 00:02:05.291
seems to say that the Russians

00:02:05.291 --> 00:02:07.627
were very deliberate
in flying in front of the drone,

00:02:07.794 --> 00:02:10.763
dumping fuel in front of the drone
and then damaging the propeller,

00:02:10.763 --> 00:02:13.333
forcing it down
eventually in the Black Sea.

00:02:13.366 --> 00:02:14.868
So now we'll wait to see how the U.S.

00:02:14.868 --> 00:02:16.803
chooses to respond to this incident.

00:02:16.803 --> 00:02:20.173
We have also reached out to the Russian
Ministry of Defense for comment, Brianna.

00:02:20.540 --> 00:02:23.676
In Orange, just to be clear, of course,
the Ukrainian port city of Odessa

00:02:23.676 --> 00:02:28.047
there on the Black Sea, we don't know
specifically where this happened.

00:02:29.149 --> 00:02:30.583
It's our understanding and it's worth

00:02:30.583 --> 00:02:32.652
noting that we have been able
to track the flights

00:02:32.652 --> 00:02:35.822
of many Reaper drones over the Black Sea
over the course of the war and before.

00:02:36.022 --> 00:02:38.491
And they essentially fly
an almost circular pattern,

00:02:38.691 --> 00:02:40.527
either
in the western part of the Black Sea,

00:02:40.527 --> 00:02:43.429
either west of Crimea
or south west of Crimea.

00:02:43.463 --> 00:02:46.766
We don't know exactly where this happened,
but we have seen Reaper drones

00:02:46.766 --> 00:02:49.836
flying almost on a daily basis
since the beginning of the war.

00:02:49.836 --> 00:02:52.739
And even earlier than that,
we know Russian jets have flown as well.

00:02:52.906 --> 00:02:53.673
Of course, what's different

00:02:53.673 --> 00:02:57.010
here is the interaction,
frankly, the collision between these jets.

00:02:57.544 --> 00:03:00.914
U.S. Air Force says it happened
in international waters where both the US

00:03:00.914 --> 00:03:02.715
and the Russians are absolutely entitled

00:03:02.715 --> 00:03:06.286
to fly under international law,
but not like this, Brianna.

00:03:06.619 --> 00:03:07.253
Certainly not.

00:03:07.253 --> 00:03:07.487
All right.

00:03:07.487 --> 00:03:09.589
Oren Liebermann,
live for us at the Pentagon.

00:03:09.589 --> 00:03:10.557
Thank you.

00:03:10.557 --> 00:03:13.793
Let's talk about this now
with General Mark Hertling.

00:03:13.793 --> 00:03:15.862
He is a CNN military analyst,

00:03:15.862 --> 00:03:19.465
former commanding general, U.S.,
your Army, Europe and Seventh Army.

00:03:19.732 --> 00:03:21.734
And David Sanger is with us as well.

00:03:21.734 --> 00:03:23.803
He is the White House
and national security

00:03:23.803 --> 00:03:25.872
correspondent for The New York Times.

00:03:25.872 --> 00:03:31.044
All right, General, first off, I mean,
just explain how significant this is.

00:03:32.111 --> 00:03:32.879
This is

00:03:32.879 --> 00:03:37.083
typical of shadowing and intercepts
in Europe.

00:03:37.350 --> 00:03:40.987
Brianna, truthfully,
what you see is Russia

00:03:40.987 --> 00:03:44.324
does this all the time
in international airspace.

00:03:45.925 --> 00:03:50.463
On top of international waters,
Russia often considers the Black Sea

00:03:50.463 --> 00:03:54.634
their national lake, which is dead wrong
and doesn't apply that way.

00:03:55.168 --> 00:03:58.338
But you will see Russian aircraft
continuously

00:03:58.938 --> 00:04:01.574
having these kinds of intercepts
or shadows,

00:04:02.375 --> 00:04:04.644
but nothing like this.

00:04:04.644 --> 00:04:08.248
Airplanes get close
You certainly will see.

00:04:08.615 --> 00:04:11.884
There have been years
where there are over a couple of hundred

00:04:12.185 --> 00:04:14.954
of these kind of things, incidents
occurring every year.

00:04:14.954 --> 00:04:16.723
And it's normal procedure.

00:04:16.723 --> 00:04:18.258
But when you get this close

00:04:18.258 --> 00:04:21.361
and you interfere
with flight paths of other aircraft,

00:04:21.361 --> 00:04:25.465
either manned or unmanned, it's
certainly not under international law.

00:04:25.498 --> 00:04:29.602
And it's certainly going to create
quite a distraction in this campaign.

00:04:29.802 --> 00:04:33.406
But as Orange is said, it's in Western,
possibly in western

00:04:33.740 --> 00:04:37.710
Black Sea region to the west
of the autonomous region of Crimea.

00:04:38.144 --> 00:04:42.181
It's just Russia, again,
interfering in international airspace

00:04:42.181 --> 00:04:43.616
with other aircraft.

00:04:43.616 --> 00:04:45.618
David, how do you think the U.S.

00:04:45.618 --> 00:04:49.455
government is looking at this as they're
trying to figure out how to respond?

00:04:51.124 --> 00:04:52.025
Well, I'm pretty

00:04:52.025 --> 00:04:55.028
sure, Brianna, they're going to respond
pretty calmly to it.

00:04:55.028 --> 00:04:58.698
I think they will denounce it,
but it's an unmanned aircraft,

00:04:58.698 --> 00:05:01.534
and that means that fortunately
there are no casualties.

00:05:01.901 --> 00:05:05.672
But I'm sure that President Biden
is going to be thinking that what he's

00:05:05.672 --> 00:05:09.976
trying to avoid here is, of course,
is an escalation with the Russians.

00:05:09.976 --> 00:05:14.647
Remember, his first goal in this war
has been help the Ukrainians

00:05:14.914 --> 00:05:19.519
His second goal in this war
has been avoid escalation

00:05:19.519 --> 00:05:21.721
and anything that could lead to World
War Three.

00:05:22.088 --> 00:05:26.659
Now, we've had surveillance craft
taken down before.

00:05:26.993 --> 00:05:30.163
The most famous case in modern times

00:05:30.496 --> 00:05:33.299
was a Chinese collision

00:05:33.599 --> 00:05:36.502
with a manned American

00:05:36.502 --> 00:05:38.971
surveillance craft
in international waters.

00:05:39.305 --> 00:05:44.410
As in this case, the Chinese pilot
ended up being killed in that incident.

00:05:44.811 --> 00:05:49.148
And the Americans survived
but were taken captive

00:05:49.148 --> 00:05:51.884
for a while,
eventually returned to the United States.

00:05:52.218 --> 00:05:55.955
This does not rise quite to that level
because it's unmanned,

00:05:56.322 --> 00:05:59.926
but it nonetheless tells you
that the Russians are now willing

00:05:59.926 --> 00:06:04.731
to take more risks to push back
on the American involvement in the war.

00:06:05.098 --> 00:06:06.632
And the question is, where does that end?

00:06:07.734 --> 00:06:09.268
You know, where does it end?

00:06:09.268 --> 00:06:10.336
And certainly the U.S.

00:06:10.336 --> 00:06:14.040
is considered with escalation, concerned
about potential escalation

00:06:14.173 --> 00:06:16.376
in here,
as we hear from the Air Force General.

00:06:16.376 --> 00:06:18.378
But I wonder
if that isn't sort of the point.

00:06:18.378 --> 00:06:21.914
And I also wonder
if from Vladimir Putin's perspective,

00:06:22.181 --> 00:06:26.452
you know, something like this
happening in the black sea is perhaps

00:06:26.853 --> 00:06:30.556
good for him, a place
where he has suffered some embarrassment.

00:06:30.590 --> 00:06:30.823
Right.

00:06:30.823 --> 00:06:34.394
When you think about the flagship
of the Black Sea fleet being sunk

00:06:37.363 --> 00:06:40.666
I would not agree with that.

00:06:40.733 --> 00:06:41.367
I'm sorry.

00:06:41.367 --> 00:06:42.568
Go ahead, David.

00:06:44.637 --> 00:06:45.405
Please, Mark. Go.

00:06:45.405 --> 00:06:46.472
Go right ahead.

00:06:46.839 --> 00:06:49.208
No, I would not agree with that.

00:06:49.208 --> 00:06:51.310
Brianna, I think this is baiting.

00:06:51.944 --> 00:06:54.147
I think a pilot made a mistake.

00:06:54.313 --> 00:06:58.751
They were trying to launch said intercept,
which means escort

00:06:58.751 --> 00:07:00.286
and see what's going on.

00:07:00.286 --> 00:07:04.056
But when you clip an aircraft
because it's to

00:07:04.223 --> 00:07:07.860
to either land or crash, then you've got

00:07:08.060 --> 00:07:10.630
you've got a different situation right
now. Yes.

00:07:10.930 --> 00:07:14.133
Russia has certainly been embarrassed
in the Black Sea with the sinking

00:07:14.133 --> 00:07:17.837
of several vessels by a country
that doesn't have the Navy that Ukraine.

00:07:18.104 --> 00:07:21.674
But certainly when you're interfering
with international aircraft

00:07:21.674 --> 00:07:24.811
in international airspace,
that's not purposeful.

00:07:25.278 --> 00:07:27.580
That's
that's beating and it's interception.

00:07:28.514 --> 00:07:31.951
You know, this is not something
that where, again, Mr.

00:07:31.951 --> 00:07:34.754
Putin is trying to puff up his chest
a little bit and says,

00:07:34.921 --> 00:07:37.190
see what I can control in the Black Sea.

00:07:37.356 --> 00:07:41.727
These Reapers were more than likely
not only looking for intelligence,

00:07:41.727 --> 00:07:45.565
but also over watching some of the grain
and fleets that are going through

00:07:45.665 --> 00:07:51.871
embargoed territory out of Ukraine
into the Bosphorus and up the down canal.

00:07:52.071 --> 00:07:55.741
So these are things
that are all parts of this.

00:07:55.942 --> 00:07:56.309
Again,

00:07:56.309 --> 00:07:59.579
all of this is conjecture on my part,
what that reaper was doing there.

00:07:59.779 --> 00:08:02.782
But certainly when a Russian aircraft
interferes clips

00:08:02.782 --> 00:08:06.486
it and knocks it out of the sky,
that's a little bit more serious.

00:08:06.652 --> 00:08:10.189
And we haven't seen one of those things
happen since this war began.

00:08:10.923 --> 00:08:12.391
This is incredibly serious.

00:08:12.391 --> 00:08:16.796
And I wonder, David,
how Vladimir Putin might respond

00:08:16.796 --> 00:08:21.467
to this versus
how he might see this as something

00:08:21.667 --> 00:08:26.873
that obvious should be avoided,
but how he might respond to this?

00:08:27.507 --> 00:08:28.307
You wouldn't expect

00:08:28.307 --> 00:08:32.078
that he's going to come out and give some
heartfelt apology to the U.S.

00:08:33.546 --> 00:08:34.981
No, he's certainly not.

00:08:34.981 --> 00:08:41.153
And, you know, think about the more recent
case of the balloon, really

00:08:41.153 --> 00:08:45.424
another kind of surveillance vehicle
that was over U.S.

00:08:45.424 --> 00:08:48.594
territory and China complained
when the U.S.

00:08:48.628 --> 00:08:49.428
took it down.

00:08:49.428 --> 00:08:52.832
But, of course, in that case,
it was clearly overt U.S.

00:08:52.832 --> 00:08:53.733
territory.

00:08:53.733 --> 00:08:56.702
The key part here is
this was in international waters.

00:08:57.103 --> 00:08:59.972
One of the big questions
that Mark raises here

00:08:59.972 --> 00:09:04.310
and you do as well is
what's the level of intent?

00:09:04.510 --> 00:09:07.413
In other words,
did Putin himself order this?

00:09:07.446 --> 00:09:09.782
Did the Russian military order this?

00:09:09.782 --> 00:09:11.951
Was this a Russian pilot

00:09:11.951 --> 00:09:16.088
who sought an opportunity
and was sort of acting on his own?

00:09:16.489 --> 00:09:21.594
We may not know that or we may take us
a while to go figure that out.

00:09:22.495 --> 00:09:24.630
My guess is that right now

00:09:24.630 --> 00:09:27.199
the administration will denounce it,

00:09:27.833 --> 00:09:31.437
but that you won't see them
take a similar action.

00:09:31.837 --> 00:09:33.973
And the reason for that is pretty clear.

00:09:33.973 --> 00:09:36.943
Putin has until now been pretty cautious

00:09:36.943 --> 00:09:40.546
about keeping the war inside
Ukrainian territory.

00:09:40.846 --> 00:09:43.215
There have been
some cyber attacks on Poland.

00:09:43.583 --> 00:09:46.152
But other than that,
there has really been no case.

00:09:46.152 --> 00:09:50.089
We've seen where they've gone into NATO's
territory, where they've gelled into

00:09:51.090 --> 00:09:52.024
that kind of territory.

00:09:52.024 --> 00:09:54.961
And I don't think Putin
wants to bring Naito into this.

00:09:55.428 --> 00:09:59.765
So my guess is that both
sides will probably cool it down,

00:09:59.966 --> 00:10:02.134
even while declaring
themselves in the right.

